= Introduction

- Patients suffering from critical illnesses have been found to be at an increased risk of hyperglycaemia
- Traditional intensive insulin therapy aimed to tightly control blood glucose under 6.106 mmol/L
- Review of the administration of intensive insulin therapy identified a significant increase of cases of hypoglycaemia in patients
- Model-based methods of glycaemic control have been introduced to better capture dynamic blood glucose fluctuations